:"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Stages (Section 6(c)/12(d)(1)/17(b) exemptive relief):**\n\n1. **Application:** File on EDGAR under Rule 0-2, followed by staff comments and amendments. Standard review has no fixed deadline. Rule 0-5 sets a staff comment target, not a guarantee.\n2. **Notice:** Once staff is satisfied, the SEC issues a notice (Federal Register/release) with a hearing-request deadline, typically about 25 days.\n3. **Order:** If no hearing is requested, staff usually grants the order under delegated authority. If one is requested, the SEC may hold a hearing or decide the matter itself.\n\n**Rule 0-5(d) expedited review:** Available when the application is substantially identical to two precedent applications granted within the prior two years. It requires a marked comparison and a certification. Novel terms are ineligible.\n\n**The 45-day clock:** Notice is targeted within 45 days of filing. Staff can extend it, toll it for amendments, or move the application to standard review. It measures time to **notice**, not to the final order.","ttft_ms":4663,"type":"result","duration_ms":7184,"uuid":"1c87afc1-0882-4897-9254-adc302863a47","ttft_stream_ms":1794,"time_to_request_ms":56,"first_content_frame_ms":1794,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
